The SpacemiT K3 SoC integrates two DDR controllers, each paired with a
Synopsys DDR PHY, supporting LPDDR4X and LPDDR5 memory. Add an SPL RAM
driver with initial support for LPDDR5 to configure both controllers
and PHYs, run training, and report the combined capacity through the
RAM uclass.

The board code must read the DDR part number from EEPROM and populate
the driver's platform data before probing the device. The driver uses
this part number to select the corresponding memory profile.

Preserve the vendor register tables, part-specific overrides and PHY
write sequence. Package the PMU IMEM firmware as an external binary
through binman.

Signed-off-by: Junhui Liu <junhui.liu@pigmoral.tech>
